                                "sense_id": "9415b610-ff92-380e-abd9-2aa861ad39fe",
                                "text": "Females of Delta campaniforme esuriens do not attack chrysidids that are breaking into their nests, but parasitism will cause them to abandon the nest (Jayakar and Spurway 1968)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "849b4ebd-374d-4a75-845c-134a4ce6ae06",
                                "sense_id": "9415b610-ff92-380e-abd9-2aa861ad39fe",
                                "text": "Chrysidids (3000 species) are especially diverse in temperate deserts of both hemispheres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90bfd9bc-f162-4817-8b39-2d6df1609943",
                                "sense_id": "9415b610-ff92-380e-abd9-2aa861ad39fe",
                                "text": "2006, Lynn Siri Kimsey, California Cuckoo Wasps in the Family Chrysididae (Hymenoptera), Entomology: Volume 125, University of California Press, page 4,\nSpecies of Argochrysis exhibit an unusual behavior not seen in other chrysidids or parasitoids."
